  "limitations": [
    "This report covers phase-1 recovery db3 vs 290, and only the 290 scheduler baseline; it does not contain frozen scheduler-fixed protocol results.",
    "Recovery success denominator is 20 positive trials per revision; 10 deliberate negative trials are safety refusals, not failed positive recoveries or successes.",
    "unknown_outcome_injected in recovery.ts has no host/plugin restart. continuation.ts unknown_recovery_restart has 5 non-vacuous cold-host injections and restarts, but does not instrument observe-call count.",
    "Continuation recoveryHostSuccesses counts raw SDK status before the durable unknown fault. All five actual calls belong to fault injection; none demonstrates safe verified recovery completion.",
    "Price-unknown denotes uncertain selector evidence, not unknown execution outcome. Its 100-tick result cannot validate cross-restart unknown blocking.",
    "Only public-form-cycle uses the public complete plugin lifecycle in conditions.ts; its first plan snapshot is after completion, so initialPlanRows=5 is not a before-run growth measurement. Other four scenarios invoke private step with externally driven changes.",
    "Continuation model providers are deterministic stubs. JEV counts are requests to those providers; live model quality, token cost and network latency are unmeasured.",
    "Necessary reentry is the script definition based on fixed entry labels and still-unvisited declared leaf labels, not a universal causal proof for arbitrary pages.",
    "Phase-1 durationMs wraps the recovery API only; it excludes later DOM oracle probes and guarded target dispatch. Timing samples are five per scenario, sequential non-randomized runs, insufficient for robust speedup claims.",
    "Plan/pending rows are bookkeeping counts, distinct from unique unresolved UI branches; bounded tick convergence and no lost named leaves do not prove whole-site exhaustion.",
    "CPU/memory/database bytes, observation/frontier/cache construction counts, 95th/99th latency distributions, arbitrary implicit JS dependencies, live OKX coverage, and long-running invalid-scope accumulation were not measured here."
  ],
